$$
\begin{array}{c}
=\frac{1}{2} b \cdot q=\frac{1}{2} c \cdot r \\
\therefore \quad \frac{1}{p}=\frac{a}{2 S}, \frac{1}{q}=\frac{b}{2 S}, \frac{1}{r}=\frac{c}{2 S} \\
\therefore \quad \frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{q}+\frac{1}{r}=\frac{1}{2 S}(a+b+c)=\frac{2 t}{2 S}=\frac{t}{S}
\end{array}
$$
